<p>Norway closed out the 2026 Milan-Cortina Winter Olympics on top of the medal table, leading all nations in both golds and total medals as the Games wrapped up in Italy. Several outlets pointed to the same familiar engine: Norway’s ski-focused programs delivering again, with cross-country star Johannes Høsflot Klæbo at the center of the haul. The closing ceremony took place at Verona Arena, where organizers handed the Olympic flag to the next Winter Games hosts in the French Alps. In the final standings, the United States finished second with 12 golds and 33 total medals, while Norway set a Winter Games record with 18 golds and ended with 41 medals overall.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/fxkTdcC-go-HR-5Ie18RxvxWOStBVB_g39DQiNUWsea2V3trO8hAw3UFgk0E0pCCavniLTusC9ZRiOlq5lhjRa18F3laVwWJXvz-ZepvzquXGsR8oCF3XYyXmnBlu_c68w0qKYup_dWB_LvCXk7HjBvq8GcPDhorFwR2YkmqsSLA6lRXBv5Yo-ee2RQeOLwC0T1d2F6jeb-RN4r9' alt='Patrons watch the Winter Olympics closing ceremony at a sports bar in Tromsø, Norway.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Participation model: The Guardian highlighted Norway’s emphasis on broad participation in sport as part of the foundation for its Winter Games success.</li><li>Other national bests: The Guardian reported that the USA, Great Britain and Australia also set team records at these Games.</li><li>US benchmark debate: The Christian Science Monitor posed a straightforward question about the U.S. result—does this count as the country’s best Winter Olympics performance?</li><li>Ski engine: Semafor credited Norway’s edge to its continued dominance in ski-based events, where cross-country and related disciplines power much of its Winter Games success.</li><li>Closing ceremony handover: At the closing ceremony in Verona Arena, organizers passed the Olympic flag to the French Alps hosts for the 2030 Winter Olympics.</li></ul><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Semafor analysis: Semafor framed Norway’s overall win as the result of sustained dominance in ski events, with cross-country and other on-snow disciplines doing much of the heavy lifting. (<a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/22/2026/norway-cleans-up-at-winter-olympics-thanks-to-dominance-on-skis'>Semafor</a>)</li><li>The Guardian: The Guardian drew a sharp contrast in scale—Norway (5.7 million) finishing ahead of the U.S. (342 million)—and pointed to Norway’s emphasis on participation in sport. (<a href='https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/feb/22/winter-olympics-2026-medal-table-standings-norway'>The Guardian</a>)</li><li>Christian Science Monitor: The Christian Science Monitor treated the U.S. finish as a measuring stick, asking whether this should be considered the country’s best Winter Olympics showing. (<a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/olympics/2026/0222/winter-olympics-final-medal-count-2026'>The Christian Science Monitor</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.cbsnews.com/news/olympic-medal-count-2026-winter-games/'>See the Olympic medal count for the 2026 Winter Games</a> - cbsnews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.semafor.com/article/02/22/2026/norway-cleans-up-at-winter-olympics-thanks-to-dominance-on-skis'>Norway cleans up at Winter Olympics thanks to dominance on skis</a> - semafor.com</li><li><a href='https://www.nytimes.com/2026/02/22/world/europe/2026-winter-olympics-klaebo-norway-epstein.html'>Johannes Hoesflot Klaebo Leads Norway to Record Olympic Medal Haul</a> - nytimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/sport/2026/feb/22/winter-olympics-2026-medal-table-standings-norway'>Norway (population: 5.7m) beats US (342m) to top Winter Olympics medal table</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='http://www.euronews.com/2026/02/23/norway-tops-the-medals-count-as-milan-cortina-olympics-close-in-verona-arena'>Norway tops the medals count as Milan-Cortina Olympics close in Verona Arena</a> - euronews.com</li><li><a href='https://www.csmonitor.com/World/olympics/2026/0222/winter-olympics-final-medal-count-2026'>